  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Chronozoa's last ability creates two Chronozoa tokens that each enter with three time counters and have all of Chronozoa's abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "29ccf76e-dfa3-4144-8ec2-6d56ae0bfa9e",
      "published_at": "2007-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Chronozoa becomes a copy of another creature and is put into the graveyard from the battlefield, no copies will be created. If another creature becomes a copy of Chronozoa and is put into a graveyard from the battlefield (with no time counters on it), two copies of Chronozoa will be created.",
      "oracle_id": "29ccf76e-dfa3-4144-8ec2-6d56ae0bfa9e",
      "published_at": "2007-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The ability checks to see if Chronozoa had no time counters on it at the time it was put into a graveyard from the battlefield. This doesn't necessarily mean it must have been sacrificed due to vanishing; it could have been put into the graveyard some other way (say, while the sacrifice ability of vanishing is on the stack).",
      "oracle_id": "29ccf76e-dfa3-4144-8ec2-6d56ae0bfa9e",
      "published_at": "2007-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you don't control any Islands when Tidewalker enters, its vanishing ability has no effect. (It enters with no time counters on it, so neither of the vanishing triggers can trigger. See \"Vanishing\" in the General Notes section above.) On the other hand, it will be 0/0 and will be put into its owner's graveyard unless something is boosting its toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "3cc857b4-3cc7-44d5-9c51-ef819d1289c6",
      "published_at": "2007-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Unless something is boosting Tidewalker's toughness, when the last time counter is removed, it will be put into the graveyard as a state-based action for having 0 toughness before it can be sacrificed as the result of vanishing.",
      "oracle_id": "3cc857b4-3cc7-44d5-9c51-ef819d1289c6",
      "published_at": "2007-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card or token enters as a copy of a permanent, the new permanent isn't kicked, even if the original was.",
      "oracle_id": "a71448ce-8d57-418e-b862-bd526726074d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell's kicker cost was paid, the spell is \"kicked.\"",
      "oracle_id": "a71448ce-8d57-418e-b862-bd526726074d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you copy a kicked spell on the stack, the copy is also kicked. If the copied spell is a permanent spell, the token the copy of that spell becomes when it enters is also kicked.",
      "oracle_id": "a71448ce-8d57-418e-b862-bd526726074d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can't kick it.",
      "oracle_id": "a71448ce-8d57-418e-b862-bd526726074d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The kicker ability doesn't let you pay a kicker cost more than once.",
      "oracle_id": "a71448ce-8d57-418e-b862-bd526726074d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine a spell's total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card's effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The spell's mana value remains unchanged, no matter what the total cost to cast it was.",
      "oracle_id": "a71448ce-8d57-418e-b862-bd526726074d",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "With a Humility and two Opalescences on the battlefield, if Humility has the latest timestamp, then all creatures are 1/1 with no abilities. If the timestamp order is Opalescence, Humility, Opalescence, the second Opalescence is 1/1, and the Humility and first Opalescence are 4/4. If Humility has the earliest timestamp, then everything is 4/4.",
      "oracle_id": "ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0",
      "published_at": "2006-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Removes all creature abilities. This includes mana abilities. Animated lands will also lose the ability to tap for mana.",
      "oracle_id": "ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0",
      "published_at": "2007-02-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is the current interaction between Humility and Opalescence:\u00a0The type-changing effect applies at layer 4, but the rest happens in the applicable layers. The rest of it will apply even if the permanent loses its ability before it's finished applying. So if Opalescence, Humility, and Worship are on the battlefield and Opalescence entered before Humility, the following is true: Layer 4: Humility and Worship each become creatures that are still enchantments. (Opalescence). Layer 6: Humility and Worship each lose their abilities. (Humility) Layer 7b: Humility becomes 4/4 and Worship becomes 4/4. (Opalescence). Humility becomes 1/1 and Worship becomes 1/1 (Humility). But if Humility entered before Opalescence, the following is true: Layer 4: Humility and Worship each become creatures that are still enchantments (Opalescence). Layer 6: Humility and Worship each lose their abilities (Humility). Layer 7b: Humility becomes 1/1 and Worship becomes 1/1 (Humility). Humility becomes 4/4 and Worship becomes 4/4 (Opalescence).",
      "oracle_id": "ed7bdb3e-5c51-4547-9266-76a791e0b2b0",
      "published_at": "2009-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
